## Definition

The abstract affective member of the kernel gmeow:MentalMoment family \(alongside cognition's gmeow:CognitiveState, epistemics' doxastic states, and teleology's gmeow:IntentionalMode\) — intrinsic affective modes inhering in one agent, so an agent's whole mental life, including what it feels, is queryable as one family \(Principles 14, 15\)\. Never instantiated directly: instances are Emotions \(the fuller model specifies Moods and affective dispositions\)\.

